    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51421" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulnĕrārĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">voln-</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		vulnus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to wounds.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">emplastrum,</span>”
				<i>a plaster for wounds</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					23, 4, 40, § 81</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">34, 11, 27,
				§ 114</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulnĕrārĭus</span></b> ,
			ii, m., <i>a surgeon</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				29, 1, 6, § 13</span></i>.</div>
